 - live cells with exactly 2 or 3 neighbors survive\n  for (const [x, y] of cells) {\n    const key = cellKey(x, y);\n    const count = neighborCounts.get(key) || 0;\n    if (count === 2 || count === 3) {\n      nextCells.push([x, y]);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Rule 4: Reproduction - dead cells with exactly 3 neighbors become alive\n  for (const [key, count] of neighborCounts.entries()) {\n    if (count === 3 && !liveCells.has(key)) {\n      const coords = key.split(',').map(Number) as [number, number];\n      const [x, y] = coords;\n      nextCells.push([x, y]);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Sort the cells to ensure consistent output order\n  // Sort by y first, then by x for consistent ordering\n  return nextCells.sort((a, b) => a[1] - b[1] || a[0] - b[0]);\n}\n```\n\n**Component Count:**\n- Constants: 2 (`0` in the empty check, `0` in neighborCounts.get) = 2\n- Bindings: 10 (cells, liveCells, neighborCounts, directions, x, y, dx, dy, neighbor, key, count, nextCells, coords, [x,y]) but counted as unique variable names = 8 unique bindings (cells, liveCells, neighborCounts, directions, nextCells, key, count, coords)\n- Invocations: 12 (cellKey, Set, map, cellKey, get, set, get, ||, [], push, entries, has, split, map, Number, as, push, sort, -, ||, -) but counting distinct function/method calls = 8 (cellKey x2, map, get x2, set, push x2, entries, has, split, map, sort) = 8\n- Conditionals: 3 (if for empty, if for survival, if for reproduction) = 3\n- Loops: 4 (for directions, for survival, for reproduction, sort) = 4\n- Assignments: 5 (liveCells, neighborCounts, directions, nextCells, coords) = 5\n\n**Total Mass:**\n(2 × 1) + (8 × 1) + (8 × 2) + (3 × 4) + (4 × 5) + (5 × 6) = 2 + 8 + 16 + 12 + 20 + 30 = 88\n\n#### **Refactoring Opportunity: Extract Constants**\n\nThe directions array is a fixed value that represents the Moore neighborhood in Conway's Game of Life. This can be extracted as a constant to improve code clarity and reusability.\n\nAdditionally, the reproduction rule count (3) appears twice in the code. This is a Game of Life rule constant that can be extracted.\n\n#### **Implementation of Refactoring**\n\n"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_12-15-39_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_qwen3-235b/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent changes: implements still life block pattern\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent changes: implements still life block pattern\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784982468402},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-81c3b9351aa72a90","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/game-of-life.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8453b8c6e4eff3ab","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/game-of-life.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":45,"output":63,"cacheRead":6576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6684,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784982468422,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-00008c30-5049-4c67-b949-64d7ddde482d","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-81c3b9351aa72a90","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"function cellKey(x: number, y: number): string {\n  return `${x},${y}`;\n}\n\nexport function nextGeneration(cells: [number, number][]): [number, number][]